 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "records are strings \"<timestamp>,task,<taskId>,<taskName>\" (root task) or \"<timestamp>,subtask,<parentId>,<taskId>,<taskName>\". The timestamp is opaque and ignored. Display the forest depth-first in pre-order: roots in record order, the children of each task in record order (a child may be recorded before its parent). Each displayed line is two spaces per depth level followed by the task name. Level 2 adds robustness: a record is skipped when its type is unknown, its field count is wrong for its type, or its id or name is empty; a later definition of an already defined task id is ignored; a subtask whose parent is never defined (or that is its own ancestor) is not displayed, nor are its descendants. Level 3 prefixes each name with its outline number and a space: the root at sibling position i (1-based) is \"i\", its j-th displayed child is \"i.j\", and so on.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk06-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
